  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF BEIRUT (1912)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Battle of Beirut in 1912 was a naval engagement during the Italo-Turkish War, involving Italian and Ottoman forces, resulting in the annihilation of Ottoman naval forces in the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALO-TURKISH WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Italo-Turkish War was a conflict between Italy and the Ottoman Empire, with the Battle of Beirut (1912) as one of its naval engagements."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUEZ CANAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Suez Canal is a waterway in Egypt, threatened by the Ottoman naval forces during the Italo-Turkish War."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALIAN NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Italian Navy played a crucial role in the Battle of Beirut (1912), attacking and destroying Ottoman naval forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTTOMAN NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ottoman Navy was present in Beirut during the Italo-Turkish War, facing destruction by the Italian Navy in the Battle of Beirut (1912)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEIRUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beirut is a city on the coast of Lebanon, where the Battle of Beirut (1912) took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF BEIRUT (1941)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Battle of Beirut in 1941 was a naval engagement during World War II, marking the end of hostilities in the Syria-Lebanon campaign, involving Allied and Vichy French forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War II was a global conflict involving multiple nations, with the Battle of Beirut (1941) as one of its naval engagements."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUSTRALIAN 7TH DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Australian 7th Division was part of the Allied forces during the Battle of Beirut (1941), contributing to the campaign in Syria-Lebanon."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Australian 7th Division was part of the Allied forces during the Battle of Beirut (1941)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VICHY FRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vichy France was a puppet state during World War II, involved in the Battle of Beirut (1941) as the opposing side to the Allies."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLAUS BARBIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klaus Barbie was a Nazi war criminal, not directly involved in the Battle of Beirut, but mentioned in the context of World War II events."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSAMA BIN LADEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osama bin Laden was a terrorist leader, not directly involved in the Battle of Beirut, but mentioned in the context of the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIEGE OF BEIRUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Siege of Beirut in 1982 was part of the 1982 Lebanon War, resulting in the displacement of Palestinian Liberation Organization (PLO) forces and cited by Osama bin Laden as a reason for the September 11, 2001, attacks."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALESTINIAN LIBERATION ORGANIZATION (PLO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PLO was displaced from Beirut during the Siege of Beirut, establishing new headquarters in Tunis."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEBANON WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Lebanon War in 1982 was a conflict involving various factions, including the PLO, resulting in the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israel was involved in the Siege of Beirut, targeting Syrian strongholds and engaging in offensive operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Syria was a party in the Siege of Beirut, defending against Israeli offensive operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEKAA VALLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Bekaa Valley is a region in Lebanon where Israeli forces engaged Syrian positions during the Battle of Beirut (1941)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Bekaa Valley is a region in Lebanon, where Israeli forces engaged Syrian positions during the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARAFAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yasser Arafat was the leader of the Palestinian Liberation Organization (PLO) and fled to Greece and then to Tunis after the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREECE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greece is a country where Arafat fled to after the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUNIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tunis is a city where Arafat established a new headquarters after fleeing from Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YEMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yemen is a location where PLO 'fedayeen' continued to operate after the Siege of Beirut."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JORDAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
